targets.display_text:
They have hands and will not feel;
feet, and will not walk;
they will not sound with their throat.

He brings clouds up from the earth’s extremity;
He made lightning for rain;
He brings winds out of His treasuries.

Do not remember our ancient acts of lawlessness;
let Thy compassions swiftly reach us first,
for we became very poor.

Remember Thy congregation, which Thou didst acquire from the beginning;
Thou didst redeem the rod of Thine inheritance,
this Mount Zion, where Thou didst encamp.

You who love the Lord, hate evil!
The Lord guards the souls of His holy ones;
He will rescue them from the hand of sinners.

You priests, speak to the heart of Jerusalem; comfort her.
For her humiliation is fulfilled, her sin is loosed;
for from the hand of the Lord she has received double for her sins.
